<!-- ═══════════════ THREE MODES ═══════════════ -->
<section id="modes">
  <h2>One binary. Three ways to use it.</h2>
  <p class="section-sub">Runs local for all three. No server, no GPU, no account.</p>

  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-tag">mode 1 - describe</div>
      <h3>Any image -> coordinates</h3>
      <p>Capture once, pipe anywhere - to MCP clients or any CLI tool. The output is typed elements with exact pixel coordinates, not a description.</p>
      <div class="card-code">
        $ farscry screen.png<br />
        -> button  "Save"       at (400,300)  enabled:true<br />
        -> input   "Email"      at (200,180)  empty:true<br />
        -> error   "Card declined"  at (20,350)
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-tag">mode 2 - diff</div>
      <h3>What changed between states</h3>
      <p>Run before and after an action. Get only what changed: which button flipped state, which field appeared, what error resolved. Deterministic. Offline. ~175 tokens avg.</p>
      <div class="card-code">
        farscry diff before.png after.png<br />
        -> button "Submit": disabled -> enabled<br />
        -> spinner: removed
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-tag">mode 3 - pipe</div>
      <h3>Cmd+Shift+4, pipe, done</h3>
      <p>Capture a region with your system hotkey. Pipe directly to your workflow. Zero file saving. Zero path typing. Zero friction between seeing a problem and fixing it.</p>
      <div class="card-code">farscry --from-clipboard | your-runner "fix this"</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="divider" />

<!-- ═══════════════ INSTALL ═══════════════ -->
<section id="install">
  <h2>Up in 30 seconds.</h2>
  <p class="section-sub">OCR assets (~12MB English) download to <code style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:0.875em;color:var(--accent-high)">~/.farscry/models/</code> on first run. No account needed.</p>

  <div class="install-ways">
    <div class="install-way">
      <h3>Auto-setup</h3>
      <p>Detects MCP clients and compatible editors automatically. Asks permission, then wires farscry into your workflow image pipeline in 30 seconds.</p>
      <div class="card-code">farscry setup</div>
    </div>
    <div class="install-way">
      <h3>Clipboard shortcut</h3>
      <p>Cmd+Shift+4 to capture a region, then paste into your workflow. farscry turns the image into structured context before the workflow has to reason over pixels.</p>
      <div class="card-code">farscry --from-clipboard</div>
    </div>
    <div class="install-way">
      <h3>MCP server</h3>
      <p>Expose farscry as an MCP tool. Your workflow calls it directly when it needs to understand an image, with no manual piping required.</p>
      <div class="card-code">farscry serve --mcp</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="code-block">
    <span class="c"># npm (TypeScript / Node.js)</span><br />
    <span class="cm">npm install -g farscry</span>
    <br /><br />
    <span class="c"># pip (Python)</span><br />
    <span class="cm">pip install farscry</span>
    <br /><br />
    <span class="c"># curl (any platform)</span><br />
    <span class="cm">curl -fsSL https:
    <br /><br />
    <span class="c"># then: auto-detect MCP clients, wire up in 30 seconds</span><br />
    <span class="cm">farscry setup</span>
  </div>
</section>

